[1.537,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[38;5;174m ▝▝   ▝▝ \u001b[12G\u001b[38;5;246m/work\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;246m❯ \u001b[38;5;231mPlease implement this issue.\u001b[39m                                                            \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m#58 A reminder list for accounting\u001b[39m                                                      \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mEvery Monday accounting sends payment reminders. Today they go through the aging report\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mby hand and copy the invoices into a spreadsheet for their mail merge. They want \u001b[39m       \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231minvoicer to print that list.\u001b[39m                                                            \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mAdd a command \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer reminders <file> [--today YYYY-MM-DD]\u001b[38;5;231m that prints the list as \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mCSV.\u001b[39m                                                                                    \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mAcceptance criteria:\u001b[39m                                                                    \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m- AC1. A row for each unpaid invoice whose due date is before today (\u001b[38;5;153m--today\u001b[38;5;231m, or the \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mcurrent date without it).\u001b[39m                                                               \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m- AC2. The first line is the header \u001b[38;5;153minvoice,customer,due_on,days_overdue,amount\u001b[38;5;231m, and \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231meach row has those columns in that order: the invoice's id, the customer's name, the \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mdue date, the number of days since the due date, and the invoice's total as \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;153mcsv\u001b[38;5;231m prints it.\u001b[39m                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m- AC3. The most overdue invoices come first; invoices overdue by the same number of \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mdays are in the order of their ids.\u001b[39m                                                     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m- AC4. An invoice overdue by more than 90 days is left out: it has gone to the \u001b[39m         \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mcollection agency, and accounting calls the agency themselves.\u001b[39m                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m- AC5. With nothing to remind, the output is the header line alone.\u001b[39m                     \r\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;5;174m✢\u001b[3G\u001b[38;5;216mKer\u001b[38;5;174mfuffling… \r\u001b[3B\u001b[38;5;246m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[7m \u001b[27m\u001b[K\u001b[34;1H\u001b[32;3H"]
