[0.027,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;246m❯ \u001b[38;5;231mPlease implement this issue.\u001b[39m                                                            \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m#58 A re\u001b[12Ginder list for accounting\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BEvery\u001b[9GMonday accounting\u001b[27Gsends payment reminders. Today they go through the aging report\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bby hand and copy the invoices into a spreadsheet for their mail merge. They want \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Binvoicer to print that list.\u001b[39m                                                           \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B                                                                                 \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231mAdd a command \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer reminders <file> [--today YYYY-MM-DD]\u001b[38;5;231m that prints the list as \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BCSV.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m                                                                                     \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231mAcceptance criteria:\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B- AC1. A row for e\u001b[22Gch unpaid invoice whose due date is before today (\u001b[38;5;153m--today\u001b[38;5;231m, or the \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcurrent date without it).\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B2\u001b[10GThe first\u001b[20Gline\u001b[25Gis the\u001b[32Gheader \u001b[38;5;153minvoice,customer,due_on,days_overdue,amount\u001b[38;5;231m,\u001b[84Gand\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Beach row has\u001b[16Gthose columns in that order: the invoice's id, the customer's name, the \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bdue date, the number of days\u001b[32Gsinc\u001b[37G the due date, and the invoice's total as \u001b[38;5;153mi\u001b[81Gvoicer \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcsv\u001b[38;5;231m p\u001b[9Gints it.\u001b[39m                                                                       \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m- AC3. The most ov\u001b[23Gdue\u001b[27Ginvoices come first; invoices overdue by the s\u001b[74Gme number of \u001b[39m \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231mdays are in \u001b[16Ghe order of their ids.\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B4\u001b[10GAn invoice overdue by more than 90 days is l\u001b[55Gft out: it has gone to the \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231mcollection agency, and accounting calls the agency themselves.\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B5\u001b[10GWith n\u001b[17Gthing to r\u001b[28Gmind, the output\u001b[45Gis the header line alone.\u001b[39m            \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m●\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[34;1H\u001b[32;3H"]
