[0.233,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[48;5;237m  \u001b[38;5;231m#58 A reminder list for accounting\u001b[39m                                                      \r\u001b[1B                              \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231mEvery Monday accounting sends payment reminders. Today they go through the aging report\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bby hand and copy the invoi\u001b[30Ges into a spreadsheet for their mail merge. They want \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Binvoicer to print that list.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m                                                                                       \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231mAdd \u001b[8G command \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer reminders <file> [--today YYYY-MM-DD]\u001b[38;5;231m that prints the list as \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BCSV.\u001b[39m                        \r\u001b[3C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;231mcceptance criteria:\u001b[39m                                                                 \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B    \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m- AC1. A row for each unpaid invoice whose due date is before today (\u001b[38;5;153m--today\u001b[38;5;231m, or the \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcurrent date without it).\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- AC2. The first line is the header \u001b[38;5;153minvoice,customer,due_on,days_overdue,amount\u001b[38;5;231m, and \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Beach row\u001b[12Ghas\u001b[16Gthos\u001b[21G \u001b[23Gol\u001b[26Gmns in that order: the invoice's id, the customer's name,\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bd\u001b[5Ge da\u001b[10Ge, \u001b[14Ghe number\u001b[24Gof days since the due date, and the invoice's total as \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcsv\u001b[38;5;231m prints\u001b[14Git.\u001b[39m                                                                       \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m- AC3. The most overdue invoices come firs\u001b[46G; invoices overdue by the same numb\u001b[82Gr\u001b[84Gof \u001b[39m \r\u001b[3C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231mays \u001b[9Gr\u001b[11G in the order of their ids.\u001b[39m     