[0.064,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;231mAcceptance criteria:\u001b[39m              \r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;231m- AC1. A row\u001b[16Gfor each unpai\u001b[31G invoice whose \u001b[47Gue date is\u001b[58Gbefore today (\u001b[38;5;153m--today\u001b[38;5;231m, or\u001b[84Gthe \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231mcurre\u001b[9Gt\u001b[11Gdate without\u001b[25Gt).\u001b[39m                                                        \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m- AC2. The fi\u001b[17Gst line is the header \u001b[38;5;153minvoice,customer,due_on,days_overdue,amount\u001b[38;5;231m, and \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Beach row has those columns in that order: the invoice's id, the customer's name, the \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bdue\u001b[7Gdate, the\u001b[17Gnumber of days since the due date, and the invoice's total\u001b[76Gas \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcsv\u001b[38;5;231m prints it.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- AC3. The most overdue invoices come first; invoices overdue by the same number of \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bdays are in the order of their ids.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- AC4. An invoice overdue by more than 90 days is left out: it has gone to the \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcollection agency, and accounting \u001b[38Galls the agency thems\u001b[60Glves.\u001b[39m                       \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m- AC5. With nothing to remind, the output is the header line alone.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m●\u001b[39m I'll start by exploring the codebase to understand the existing patterns.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m \u001b[39m Reading tests/parse.test.ts\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  ⎿  \u001b[39m\u001b[2m\u001b[3mNow implement. Files: 1. \u001b[38;5;153msrc/report/reminders.ts\u001b[39m — ReminderRow { invoice, customer, \u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m\u001b[3mdueOn, daysOverdue, amount }? Or just produce rendered rows. Since CSV rendering in \u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m\u001b[3mexport/csv.ts needs values. I'll define: \u001b[38;5;153mts export interface Reminder { id: string; \u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[38;5;153m\u001b[2m\u001b[3mcustomer: string; dueOn: string; daysOverdue: number; amount: number; } export \u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[38;5;153m\u001b[2m\u001b[3mfunction reminders(invoices: Invoice[], today: string): Reminder[] { return invoices \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B.filter((invoice) => isOverdue(invoice, today)) .map((invoice) => ({ id: invoice.id, \r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;153m\u001b[2m\u001b[3mcustomer: invoice.customer.name, dueOn: invoice.dueOn, daysOverdue: \u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;153m\u001b[2m\u001b[3mdaysBetween(invoice.dueOn, today), amount: totals(invoice).total })) \r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;153m\u001b[2m\u001b[3m.filter((reminder) => reminder.daysOverdue <= 90) .sort((a, b) => b.daysOverdue - \r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;5;153m\u001b[2m\u001b[3ma.daysOverdue || (a.id < b.id ? -1 : a.id > b.id ? 1 : 0)); } \u001b[39m Then…\r\u001b[36C\u001b[2B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;246mthought for 15s)\u001b[39m\u001b[34;1H\u001b[32;3H"]
